Right, my mistake for stating that too strongly. So how I understand it is
that the BLUPs are (often fairly strongly) shrunk towards being normally
distributed, but that doesn't mean they're exactly normally distributed.
 The variance of the BLUPs is usually not numerically equivalent to the
estimated variance of the random effect, either, I believe for the same
reasons.

Does that jive with your understanding, Dan?

