Are you looking for a clever one-liner for clarity or are you looking to
avoid copying for memory and performance reasons? In the former case,
swap() in Kmisc provides what you want.

library(Kmisc)

x <- 1:10
x
x <- swap(x, c(2,3), c(3,2))
x
x <- swap(x, c(2,10), c(10,2))
x

In the latter case, your best bet is to compile R with
--enable-memory-profiling (OSX R does this by default) and use tracemem()
and Rprofmem().

    Hope this helps!

        Mike.


